The toy models in Sec.~\ref{sec:Toy-model} quantitatively demonstrate the efficacy of Tikhonov regularization in mitigating both uncorrelated and correlated uncertainties within discrete Fourier inversion. Based on these tests, we implement the regularization scheme to analyze the pion quasi DA from lattice QCD, specifically utilizing the bootstrap ensembles of Euclidean correlators $g(\lambda)$ generated by the Lattice Parton Collaboration (LPC) \cite{LatticeParton:2022zqc}, as illustrated in Fig.~\ref{fig:real-input-pion-quasi-DA}.

