\subsection{Collagen-modulating phenotypes display different invasion patterns}
\label{sec:4.3}

To examine the dynamics of collagen fibre degrading phenotype we set the secretion rate to zero, $s=0$. Figure~\ref{Fig4}(a) shows that faster collagen fibre degradation reduces contact guidance, with cells displaying invasion patterns similar to when no fibres are present (compare with Figure~\ref{Fig2}). We observe that a higher degradation rate promotes proliferation by facilitating dispersion of the cells (see Figure~\ref{fig:fig4_SI}(a),(b) in Supplementary Information (Section~\ref{sec: fig4_SI})).

% -------------------------------------------------------------------------

