In order to find the eigenvalues of the hydrodynamic matrix, we have to find the roots of its characteristic polynomial. We use again the simplified notation where the evaluation at the homogeneous steady state is  tacitly assumed for all quantities.  We obtain the following characteristic polynomial for the hydrodynamic matrix:

\begin{widetext}
\begin{equation}
