The chosen scaling on the derivative of $G$ is motivated by their expansion in power of $\gamma$ when $\alpha\neq 1$ which verify in our system $G_\rho = G_{\rho}^{(1)}\gamma + \dots$ and $G_T = G_T^{(0)} + G_T^{(1)}\gamma + \dots$ with $G_{\rho}^{(1)}\neq 0$ and $G_T^{(0)}\neq 0$. Proceeding with the expansion defined by Eqs.~\eqref{eq: less stupid expansion} leads to the eigenvalues:

