\subsection{Proofs}
\begin{lemma}[Proof of Theorem~\ref{ThmC} - Part 1]\label{Part1}
For each $\La_\ell$, and every two multicurves with $\iota_\cC(\mf{m}),\iota_\cC(\mf{m}')\in\La_\ell$,  the product $\mf{m} \ast \mf{m'}$ has a unique leading order term $\mf{m}_\#$ with  $\iota_\cC(\mf{m}_\#)\in \La_\ell$ satisfying 
$$
|\mf{m}_\#|= |\mf{m}|+|\mf{m}'|.
$$
\end{lemma}
\begin{proof}

Note that the modified DT coordinates are piecewise linear functions of the standard DT coordinates. More precisely, by \eqref{MDT}, the regions in which the transformation is linear are determined by the inequalities  
$$
n_i\geq n_j+n_k~~~\tn{or}~~~n_i\leq n_j+n_k
$$
in each pair of pants $F(a_i,a_j,a_k)$. These inequalities are a subset of the inequalities that determine the regions of linearity $\wt\La_\ell$ of $\iota_\cC$ in $\overline{\mc{D}}$. We conclude that:\\

{\it Over each $\wt\La_\ell$, the map from DT coordinates to modified DT coordinates is the restriction to $\wt{\La}_\ell$ of a rational linear isomorphism $\Psi_\ell\colon \R^{6g-6}\lra \R^{6g-6}$.}\\

Before we use the last observation to prove Lemma~\ref{Part1}, we need to modify the definition of leading term in \eqref{leading-term} in some special cases. Fixing one of the cones $\wt{\La}_\ell\subset \ov{\mc{D}}$, for every $i=1,\ldots,3g-3$, if $n''_i>n'_i$ over $\wt{\La}_\ell$, in Convention~\ref{new-convention}, we modified the DT coordinates of multicurves $\mf{m}$ with $n_i=0$ to have twist coordinates $t_i\leq 0$ instead of $t_i\geq 0$ in order for $\iota_\cC$ to define a continuous map from $\wt\La_\ell$ to $\La_\ell$. A similar change must be applied to the definition of leading term in \eqref{leading-term} when such $\mf{m}$ is multiplied with another multicurve $\mf{m}'$ in $\wt\La_\ell$ as follows.\\

If $n_i(\mf{m})=0$, $\mf{m}= a_i^{\tau}~\mf{m}''$ for some $\tau\geq 0$ such that both $n_i$ and $t_i$ of $\mf{m}''$ are zero. Since the argument below only concerns the $i$-th twist coordinate, we may assume $\mf{m}= a_i^{\tau}$. Then, \eqref{leading-term} states that there is a unique leading term $\mf{m}_\#$ in $a_i^{\tau}\ast \mf{m'}$ such that 
$$
\nu'(\mf{m}_\#)=\nu'(\mf{m}')+ ((0,\ldots,0), (0,\ldots,0, \tau, 0, \ldots,0);
$$
i.e. all the modified DT (as well as standard DT) coordinates of $\mf{m}_\#$ are the same as in $\mf{m}'$; only the $i$-th twist coordinate increases by $\tau$. Topologically, this leading order term is obtained as follows. The standard representative of the multicurve $\mf{m}'$ and $\tau$ copies of $a_i$ intersect at $n_i\cdot \tau$ points in the annulus $A_i$ around $a_i$; see Figure~\ref{Grid}-Left. To get $\mf{m}_\#$, all these intersection points must be resolved positively as in Figure~\ref{Grid}-Right. 
