A sphere with diameter $D$ and density $\rho_{\rm c}$ moves in this pressure-driven flow.
The fluid and the sphere are initially at rest and start to be driven by the pressure gradient.
The center of the sphere is initially located at $(x_{\rm c}, y_{\rm c}, z_{\rm c}) = (0.5L, 0.4H, 0.5H)$, slightly off the channel centerline.
We do not consider gravity, i.e., $\bm{G} = \bm{0}$.
