and are set as $U=0.01~\Delta{x}/\Delta{t}$ and $Re = 40$ with $\nu = 0.05~(\Delta{x})^2/\Delta{t}$.
The boundary points representing the sphere are almost evenly distributed in the same way as in section~\ref{sec:sphere_Poiseuille_fix}, 
and the number $N$ of the boundary points is determined so that $S/N = 1.0 (\Delta{x})^2$.
