\subsection{Tamper-Aware Copyright Message Decoding}
\label{Tamper-aware Copyright Message Extraction}
Finally, we decode copyright messages from $\widetilde{W}_{cop}$, using the refined tampering mask $\widetilde{M}_{tam}^{ref}$ as a guide to enhance robustness against tampering distortions. Specifically, we first decrypt $\widetilde{W}_{cop}$ with the original encryption key and then apply \textbf{t}amper-\textbf{a}ware \textbf{d}ecoding (TAD). By excluding watermark bits $w_c$ identified as compromised in $\widetilde{M}_{tam}^{ref}$, the system aggregates remaining reliable bits through majority voting to reconstruct $\widetilde{m}$. This selective exclusion of tampered regions significantly improves copyright message recovery accuracy under malicious modifications.

