\end{equation*}
where the subscript $jk$ is dropped, $f_{1,2}\in\mathbb{R}$ is a function of $\delta \Omega_{jk0}$ \cite{schweighart2002high}, and $z$-axis dynamics has added the term $2 l \omega_z \cos(\cdot)$ to compensate for the cross-track motion errors owing to time averaging. It is worth noting that this model includes the error disturbance by averaging, i.e., $\ddot{r}_{\mathrm{avg}jk}=(\nabla^2 U_{J_2}-
\int_0^{2\pi} \nabla^2 U_{J_2}\frac{\mathrm{d}\theta}{2\pi})$.
