\subsection{The ETF Algorithm}
The analyses and algorithms studied in Sections IV.A and IV.B can be easily integrated with an existing multi-hop multicasting algorithm, because the implementation of these results only require knowledge of the coordinates of multicasting forwarders. As mentioned, coordinates are obtainable for example via a GPS receiver or as discussed in previous studies (e.g., [18-19]), and can be piggybacked on the control packets exchanged between multicasting forwarders while establishing the multicasting architecture. In this section, we combine these results so that $m$ may efficiently choose an appropriate trajectory for the transition $A\rightarrow{B}$ under a variety of different conditions.
