Output: \> $m$'s ETF transition trajectory. \\
---------------------------------------------------------------------------\\[-6pt]
1. When establishing the multicasting architecture, all select- \\ ed
multicasting forwarders exchange the information of their \\ locations and referred coverage radii; these forwarders calcu- \\ late and exchange their Euclidean distances with each other; \\
2. $m$ decides whether $F_A$ and $F_B$ are overlapping or not ba- \\ sed on the Euclidean distance of $F_A$ and $F_B$; \\
3. If overlapping (i.e., a short-distance transition), $m$ employs \\ Theorem 1 to check seamlessness of $A\rightarrow{B}$; \\
