\section{Testbed}
We instrument the collective communication library (in this case, NCCL) to log information pertaining to the collective operations. In the current open-source implementation of NCCL, the logging functionality lacks detailed information, which is required to carry out the desired analysis. We log information pertaining to bytes exchanged between GPU pairs (along with the GPUs involved). The GPU-to-GPU field in our logs is used to determine which application is transmitting data from the source GPU to the destination GPU. 
We run DeepSeek V3 (shown in this overview), GPT2, Llama, BERT, Resnet18 and VGG11 using our customized NCCL. The setup contains 4 servers equipped with 8 NVIDIA H100 GPUs (connected using NVlink inside each server) in a rail-optimized topology. The NCCL logs are used to analyze individual workloads.  


