    %We will demonstrate our technique first for a simplistic type of policy that is based on a normal i.i.d. assumption of the asset returns. The simplicity allows us to derive analytic results and show the effectiveness of the posed method. Thereafter, we study the performance on more complex investment policies by exemplarily investigating the effects of uncertainty-awareness for AR-type policies. Due to the lack of tractability, we will thereby rely on numerical results on simulated data, and conclude with an analysis on real market data. Eventually, we will touch upon the calibration of uncertainty measures and provide an outline on how the procedure may be applied to other stochastic control problems such as hedging.
