\end{align}
see \Cref{lem:OospUAIidEntrEntr} for the analytic representation. (\oldchange{To aid clarity, whenever appropriate, we use the more lengthy notation $\Delta S_1 \sim \ccN(\mu,\sigma)$ to illustrate which random variable is distributed according to which measure.})

Alternatively, one could use $\UM := \cvar_\alpha$ (see \Cref{id:CVaR}) for uncertainty aversion $\alpha \in [0,1]$, \oldchange{where $\alpha=0$ corresponds to the worst-case measure and $\alpha=1$ represents the expectation operator.} This results in the uncertainty aware-strategy 
\begin{align}
    &\argmax_{\Strategy \in \R} 
    \cvar_{\alpha}\Big(
    \entr_\lambda
    \big(
        a \Delta S_1
        ~ \big| ~
        \Delta S_1 \sim \calN(\mu, \hat \sigma)
    \big)
    ~ \Big| ~
    \mu \sim \calN(\hat{\mu}, \hat \tau)
