In a previous study~\cite{Gao:2024leu}, we investigated the long-neglected potential of muons for quantum state tomography and Bell inequality tests, specifically in the context of $\mu^-e^-$ scattering in muon on-target experiments, utilizing a kinematic approach~\cite{PhysRevD.107.116007,Cheng:2024rxi}. In this article, we examine the case of Bhabha scattering within a similar theoretical framework. This leads to a new method for producing high-energy entangled electron-positron pairs. 
