\noindent Figure \ref{fig:orderparam} shows the results for $\phi$ versus density $\rho$. There is a transition at or close to $\rho$ = 0.5; the transition becomes sharper as the system size increases. The data resemble the behavior of an order parameter for a continuous phase transition, with $\rho_c$ = 0.5. Above the transition, we characterize the order parameter growth from a log-log plot (inset of fig \ref{fig:orderparam}): $\phi\:\sim\:|\rho -\rho_c|^{\beta}$ with critical exponent $\beta$.
