\section*{Abstract}

%This thesis investigates parallel real and irreducible spinors on an oriented and spin Lorentzian four-manifold with a view toward applications in globally hyperbolic supersymmetry and its associated Cauchy evolution flow in four dimensions. 

%This thesis applies the theory of spinorial polyforms associated to bundles of irreducible real spinors of real type to investigate parallel spinors on Lorentzian four-manifolds. Our main applications are directed to the study of torsion parallel spinors and the globally hyperbolic solutions of the \emph{supersymmetric NS-NS system}, a coupled gauge differential system inspired by supergravity that gives a natural gauge-theoretic interpretation of skew-torsion as the curvature of a curving on a abelian bundle gerbe, a natural categorification of the notion of principal circle bundle.  

In this dissertation, parallel spinors on oriented and spin Lorentzian four-manifolds are investigated using the theory of spinorial polyforms. The main applications are directed towards the study of torsion parallel spinors and the globally hyperbolic solutions of the four-dimensional supersymmetric NS-NS system. This differential system, which originates in supergravity, involves torsion parallel spinors subject to a curvature condition and provides a natural gauge-theoretic interpretation of skew-symmetric torsion as the curvature of a curving on an abelian bundle gerbe, a natural categorification of the notion of principal circle bundle.

\

\

\

\


\section*{Zusammenfassung}

Diese Arbeit befasst sich mit reelle und irreduziblen Spinoren auf einer orientierten und spin-Lorentzschen Viermannigfaltigkeit mit Blick auf Anwendungen in der global hyperbolischen Supersymmetrie und dem damit verbundenen Cauchy-Evolutionsfluss in vier Dimensionen. 


