\subsection{Further Discussion}
\textbf{Further Analysis of BFE}. 
In LRC, we integrate information from both image and text modalities based on Eq. (4) to determine cross-modal identity relationships within a batch. To verify the effectiveness of this integration approach, we conduct comparative experiments by constructing models that use only image information (LRCI) or only text information (LRCT) and evaluate their performance. As shown in Table \ref{Tab5}, when relying solely on single-modal relationships to establish cross-modal identity correspondences within a batch, although the model outperforms the baseline, its performance decreases to varying extents across different datasets compared to the B+LRC method, which utilizes both modalities. This is mainly because relying solely on single-modal relationships for cross-modal identity matching often results in inaccuracies and incompleteness, thereby limiting further performance improvements.\\

