\begin{abstract}
It is shown that shape preservation is decidable for
top-down tree transducers, bottom-up tree transducers, and for
compositions of total deterministic macro tree transducers.
Moreover, if a transducer is shape preserving, then it can be
brought into a particular normal form, where every input node
creates exactly one output node.
\end{abstract}

