\subsection{Model 2: triplet-singlet hybrid construction}
%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%

This model features distinct representation assignments where the lepton doublets $L$ and fermion singlets $S$ transform as $A_4$ triplets, while the right-handed charged leptons $E_R$ and neutrino singlets $N$ are assigned to identical $ A_4 $ singlets $\mathbf{1}$. To prevent lepton mass degeneracy despite identical representations, we implement differentiated modular weights across generations. The field transformations and weight assignments, detailed in table~\ref{tab:fieldcont2}, are chosen to exclude unwanted terms while ensuring modular invariance.
