\subsection{Implementation Details}
For a fair comparison, we use the publicly available visual and textual features following \cite{mesm, m-diff}. 
Specifically, we use CLIP+SlowFast (C+SF) \cite{clip,sf} as the video feature extractor for QVHighlights and Charades-CG, C3D \cite{c3d} for TACoS, and VGG \cite{vgg} for Charades-CD. For query features, we adopt CLIP for QVHighlights and Charades-CG, and GloVe \cite{glove} for the other two datasets. 
We set $\lambda_{kl}$ as 0.05 for TACoS, and 0.1 for QVHighlights, Charades-CD, and Charades-CG. 
The hidden dimension of the transformer layers is 256. 
We use $\lambda_{L_1} = 10$, $\lambda_{iou} = 1$, and $\lambda_{ce} = 4$ for TSG loss $\mathcal{L}_{tsg}$ as \cite{qvhighlights}. 
Our model is trained with Adam optimizer \cite{adam} with an initial learning rate of 1e-4 and weight decay 1e-4 on a single NVIDIA RTX 3090 with 12 batch size.

